From: ElementalWarrior
Date: 2026-10-12
Subject: Bridge the OpenCL 2.0 SVM API family

Export and bridge all eight SVM functions: clSVMAlloc, clSVMFree,
clSetKernelArgSVMPointer, clEnqueueSVMMemcpy, clEnqueueSVMMemFill,
clEnqueueSVMMap, clEnqueueSVMUnmap and clEnqueueSVMMigrateMem.

SVM pointers live in the shared Wine/host address space, so they cross
the bridge transparently; same append-only treatment as 0067 (spec,
param structs, unix dispatch, wrappers, PE entries). Verified with a
coarse-grain roundtrip on NVIDIA: alloc, host fill via map, kernel
through an SVM pointer arg, device copy, fill, migrate and free, with
a bit-exact readback.

